    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1113-a1">

                <pb facs="1185" n="1089" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg1089"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 15.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Ravndal to Mr.
                            Moore.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Consulate of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Beirut</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-09-28"><hi rendition="#italic">September 28,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 13.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In confirmation of my dispatch No. 11, I
                    have the honor to inclose herewith a copy of my dispatch No. 24 to the
                    consulate-general in regard to Mr. Balzer and his wife, Americans of Jewish
                    origin, who, on account of their creed, have been subject to various hardships
                    by the local Turkish authorities and are now threatened with banishment.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">G. Bie Ravndal</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">United States Consul.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
